Icecast 2.5.0's admin dashboard (/admin/dashboard.xsl) asks util_crypt_is_new_secure() whether the C library
supports a secure password hash. macOS's crypt() supports none of the hashes Icecast looks for ($6$, $5$, $1$),
so the detected algorithm stays NULL and Icecast dereferences it: the whole server crashes (SIGSEGV) as soon as
someone opens the dashboard. Treat "no algorithm found" as "not secure" instead.

--- a/src/util_crypt.c
+++ b/src/util_crypt.c
@@ -243,7 +243,7 @@
     if (pthread_once(&crypt_detect, crypt_detect_run) != 0)
         return NULL;
 
-    return new_algo->secure;
+    return new_algo && new_algo->secure;
 #else
     return false;
 #endif
